  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">α</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>!</mo><mo>)</mo><mo>!</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>!</mo><msup><mo>)</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">β</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>!</mo><mo>)</mo><mo>!</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>!</mo><msup><mo>)</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">α</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>24</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>!</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>!</mo><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>6</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">β</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>120</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>!</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>!</mo><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>24</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p>If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>24</mn></math> distinct objects are divided into <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn></math> groups of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math> objects in each group, then the number of ways of formation of group is<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>24</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>!</mo><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>6</mn></msup><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math></p><p>Similarly, let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>120</mn></math> distinct objects are divided into <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>24</mn></math> groups of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math> objects in each group.</p><p>So, the number of ways of formation of groups</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>120</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>!</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>!</mo><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>24</mn></msup><mo>·</mo><mn>24</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math></p>",
